#. type: Title =
#: ../src/production-orders.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Production Orders"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/production-orders.adoc:4
msgid "Factory gauges set to the xref:factory-gauge.adoc#production-orders[\"follow demand and order\" mode] allow their products to be manually ordered from a stock keeper tuned to the same network. In the stock keeper UI, each gauge in this mode appears as a [#term-production-task]_production task_, signified by a blueprint background."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/production-orders.adoc:9
msgid "Click to add the production task to the order. The amount of output items to send can be adjusted per usual. Sending an order containing production tasks creates a [#term-production-order]_production order_, causing the corresponding factory gauges to add the number of items in the order to their xref:factory-gauge.adoc#term-demand[demands]. When the ordered items arrive in the logistic network, they are sent out again to the address specified on the order."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: ../src/production-orders.adoc:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ordering 16 oak planks to be sent to the address \"`output`\""
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/production-orders.adoc:14
msgid "The responsible factory gauge will produce enough items to satisfy the amount specified in the production order, reusing existing items in storage. For example, if the xref:factory-gauge.adoc#term-recipe[recipe] of the gauge produces 4 oak planks from 1 oak log, and 5 oak planks are ordered when 0 oak planks are in storage, then 8 planks will be produced, 5 sent to the destination address, 3 left over in storage; when 5 planks are order again, 4 new planks will be produced, leaving 2 left-over."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: ../src/production-orders.adoc:16
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pending Production Orders"
msgstr ""

#. type: #view
#: ../src/production-orders.adoc:19
msgid "Pending production orders can be viewed in the \"production orders\" tab (❶) in the stock keeper UI. They are automatically removed when all ordered items arrive in the logistic network. Otherwise, they remain stuck if the items never arrive."
msgstr ""

